//Because a linked list doesn't support random access, I use slow and fast pointers to find the middle node. The middle becomes the root of the BST. I disconnect the left half and recursively convert the left and right halves into subtrees. This produces a height-balanced BST."
//Time: O(n) where n is the number of nodes in the linked list
//Space: O(log n) for the recursion stack in a balanced tree, O(n) for a skewed tree